1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Every Reel has a cliff — one second where most of your viewers leave. Find it and everything changes.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:11,000
DIY version: open your retention graph, find the steepest drop, and write down the timestamp. Not the average. The drop.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Now watch your own Reel and stop at that second. What’s on screen? Nine times out of ten it’s one of three things: a lane change, a promise not yet paid, or the desert from last week.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,000
Fix the cliff second before you make anything new. Repairing one post’s weakness teaches you more than shipping three more with the same one.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Want the cliff found for you, frame by frame, free? One Reel, full teardown — link’s in my bio.

